  "reason": "Evidence: multiprofile + scvi_n200 + transformer achieved the best result so far (0.653 acc), and multiprofile was the single largest gain (+0.13 over singleprofile). scvi_n200 outperformed pca_n2000 in singleprofile (0.52 vs 0.485), but scgpt remains untested. Uncertainty: we do not know whether a generative pre-trained encoder (scgpt) could surpass scvi_n200 in the multiprofile regime, or whether the 0.65 ceiling is encoder-specific. This experiment tests whether scgpt + multiprofile + transformer can push past the current best, directly exploiting the strongest known configuration while exploring the last untested RNA encoder. It is the best use of the next budget slot because it targets the most impactful remaining design axis (RNA encoder quality) within the already-validated multiprofile/transformer setting, and the outcome—whether scgpt matches, beats, or falls below scvi_n200—sharply narrows the search space for all downstream multimodal experiments."
